Project: RustVision (Hardware Input Merger / Cheat)
Platform: Dual-Pico (RP2040) Setup
Anti-Cheat Target: EAC (Rust)

[HARDWARE ARCHITECTURE]
- Pico #1 (Master): Receiver. Connected to PC via USB-to-TTL (CH340).
  - Peripheral: OLED Display 0.91/0.96 (I2C SSD1306).
  - Peripheral: Tactical Buttons (Profile switch + Panic Button).
- Pico #2 (Slave): Mouse Emulator. Connected to Gaming PC.
  - Input: Physical Mouse via Type-C OTG (using PIO USB Host 1000Hz).
  - Connection: UART Link (Pico 1 TX -> Pico 2 RX, Common Ground).

[LOGIC]
- PC Software (RustVision) sends X,Y offsets to Pico 1 via Serial.
- Pico 1 updates OLED, checks Buttons, sends data to Pico 2.
- Pico 2 merges Real Mouse movement + Offsets and sends to PC.

[SECURITY]
- Full USB Spoofing (VID/PID/Serial of real mouse).
- Physical Panic Button for instant Legit Mode.
- No COM-port or suspect devices on Gaming PC.